IMPORT prelude

-- Stamp Duties Act 1923 (SA), First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000 (SA) and Taxation Administration
-- Act 1996 (SA) -- shared nouns and helpers for the seat-neutral core.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website. Sourced from the South Australian Legislation
-- website at 10 March 2025; for the latest information on South Australian Government legislation, please go to
-- www.legislation.sa.gov.au. State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0. Taken through the Open Australian Legal Corpus
-- (Umar Butler / Isaacus, version 7.1.0, CC BY 4.0). NOT the official text, and possibly out of date: the deposited
-- texts are as at 2025-02-13 (the Stamp Duties Act and the First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act),
-- 2022-09-29 (Stamp Duties Regulations 2013), 2021-03-11 (First Home and Housing Construction Grants Regulations 2015)
-- and 2019-10-03 (Taxation Administration Act 1996). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md and NOTES.md.
--
-- Stamp Duties Act s 3 and Taxation Administration Act s 4: the Stamp Duties Act is a taxation law, administered with
-- the Taxation Administration Act, so the parties and acts of the duty rules are declared once here. The first home
-- owner grant's parties and acts are in fhog-terms.l4.
--
-- This module holds arithmetic and date helpers, the explicit "not covered" answers and the parties and acts of the
-- duty rules. It states no rule of any Act.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Shared nouns -- Stamp Duties Act 1923 and Taxation Administration Act 1996 (SA)`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- Schedule 2 clauses 2(1) and 3(1) charge "for every $100 or fractional part of $100": a part of $100 counts as a whole
-- $100.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of 100-dollar parts in` MEANS
    `the number of parts of` 100 `in` `amount`

-- The same count for any unit: Schedule 2 clause 2(3)(a) charges "for each 3 months or part of each 3 months".
GIVEN `unit` IS A NUMBER, `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of parts of` `unit` `in` `amount` MEANS
    IF `amount` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY `unit`) TIMES `unit` EQUALS `amount`
         THEN `amount` DIVIDED BY `unit`
         ELSE FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY `unit`) PLUS 1

§§ `Dates`

-- The prelude has no ordering on DATE, so days are compared by their serial numbers. `YMD` is a local shim.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD `y` `m` `d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is before` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is on or after` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is on or before` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `last` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `first` `to` `last` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `last` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `first`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `first` `and` `second` MEANS
    IF `first` `is on or before` `second` THEN `first` ELSE `second`

GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` `m` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `m` `y`)

-- "n months after" a day: the same day of the month n months later, or the last day of that month if it has no such
-- day. READING: the Acts do not say how a period of months is counted (NOTES.md, finding 13); the Acts Interpretation
-- Act 1915 is not deposited. "12 months after" a day is the same day a year later.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the lesser of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the days in month` `month` `year`)) `month` `year`
    WHERE
        `index` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `year`  MEANS FLOOR (`index` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `month` MEANS `index` MINUS (`year` TIMES 12) PLUS 1

§§ `Answers outside the deposited text`

-- Where a question reaches a formula the deposit has lost, or a date the deposit does not cover, the answer says so.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the s 71DD(7) formula for the reduction on a pre-6 June 2024 contract in the phase-out band is missing from the deposited text`
    `the s 71DB off-the-plan formula is missing from the deposited text`
    `the s 42BA formula for a transfer of registration to or from a continuing owner is missing from the deposited text`
    `the grant amounts before 15 October 2012 involve bonus grants whose formulas are missing (ss 18B, 18BA) and are not encoded`
    `the grant amount for a transaction other than a new home transaction before 1 July 2014 turns on the 2012 statutory date and is not encoded`
    `a registration period longer than 12 months is not in the Schedule 2 clause 2(3) table`

DECLARE `Duty answer` IS ONE OF
    `the amount, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the parties and the acts`

-- The parties the Stamp Duties Act and the Taxation Administration Act name. The Commissioner of State Taxation, the
-- Minister and the Supreme Court are parties to rules, never seats.
DECLARE `Duty party` IS ONE OF
    `the person who executed the instrument`
    `the purchasers`
    `a complying purchaser, the others exempted by the Commissioner`
    `the person who paid the surcharge`
    `the Commissioner`
    `the taxpayer`
    `the objector`
    `the Minister`

DECLARE `Duty act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the duty and have the instrument stamped`
    `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
    `cease to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
    `advise the purchasers in writing that relief from duty is no longer available`
    `apply for a refund of the foreign ownership surcharge`
    `refund the foreign ownership surcharge`
    `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister`
    `give written notice of the determination of the objection`
    `appeal to the Supreme Court`
    `give the Commissioner at least 14 days written notice of the intention to appeal`
